<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 10.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios-Jan 10.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Portman Min	    349.21   2.20</p>
<p> 2   Niugini Min	    220.14   3.06</p>
<p> 3   Mayne Nickless	 176.60   8.00</p>
<p> 4   Colonial Coml	  124.04   2.27</p>
<p> 5   Adel Bton Cement     122.46   1.69</p>
<p> 6   Herald Rsc		88.50   1.00</p>
<p> 7   Forrestania Gold	83.87   2.34</p>
<p> 8   Countrywide-PP	  83.21   1.14</p>
<p> 9   Westral Forest	  81.16   2.24</p>
<p>10   Energy Equity	   75.54   1.05</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Dominion Min	     1.91   0.83</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    2.97   0.84</p>
<p> 3   Computer Power	   3.83   3.92</p>
<p> 4   Premier Inv		4.40   0.78</p>
<p> 5   Queensland Cotton	5.82   4.42</p>
<p> 6   Parbury Ltd		6.59   0.78</p>
<p> 7   BTR Plc		    6.66   6.20</p>
<p> 8   Aust Gold Rsc	    7.07   1.29</p>
<p> 9   OLS Asia Hldgs	   7.23   0.86</p>
<p>10   Grosvenor tr	     7.62   1.50</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
